5,1,1,talk,Servas,,We must ensure the hands that do the work are truly there. A vision is only as strong as the people who can realize it.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Midori,,I agree. I'm also worried about whether the budget actually covers everything these days. We should check what costs are still centrally managed.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about the shared facilities! If everyone uses the same machines and they're broken, the research stops. We need to check the equipment status.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A fair point, Kenji. I'm curious about where the actual bottlenecks occur. It would be a tragedy to fund a project that spends half its time in administrative limbo.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Toshio,,Instincts can be misleading. I believe we should look at the actual delivery records of past awards to see what truly produces results.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"Wisdom teaches us that infrastructure is a tool, but the technician is the soul of the lab. Let us verify the human element.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, that's very true. I think looking into the staffing rolls and the facility rates would help us see the real cost of research.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"I want to see the incident logs for the instruments! If they are always crashing, we can't pick a project that relies on them too much.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,I'll be looking for patterns of delay. Perhaps the closeout files or the portfolio review of overruns will reveal where the ghosts in the machine hide.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree with Benjamin on the closeout files. We need to know if the promises made in the proposal were actually kept.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,Let us be thorough. I shall look into the staffing rolls and the secondment minutes to see who is actually available.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Midori,,I'll focus on the facility day rates and the national computing agreement. I want to see how much the agency still absorbs.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm going for it! I'll check the incident logs and the accreditation and bookings at shared facilities. Let's see if there's any room left!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall examine the portfolio review of schedule overruns and the closeout files. I'm hoping for a bit of transparency regarding those ""unforeseen"" delays.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Toshio,,I will examine the closeout files of finished awards and the portfolio review of schedule overruns. I want to see the reality of the delivery.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
