60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A seems the most viable. The data is there, and the work is about organization and cataloging, which is sustainable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Servas. Candidate A relies on sequencing and data, which fits perfectly with the subsidized computing and repository support.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate C is out! They need spectroscopy, and I saw those machines are broken. Candidate B is also risky because the glasshouses are full!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A is the most logical choice. It avoids the biological volatility of Candidate B and D, and the hardware risks of Candidate C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate A is a utility project. Historically, these ""atlas"" style projects are the ones that keep earning their keep long after the grant ends.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a gentle path, but a sure one. Candidate A provides a foundation for others to build upon for years to come.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"And from a budget perspective, the costs for A are the most predictable. It won't be eaten up by rising animal care fees.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm really worried about Candidate D too. Salamanders need a lot of care, and if the staff is stretched thin, the animals might suffer.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. The ""regeneration"" of the project's timeline in Candidate D would be a miracle given the current staffing and facility trends.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"I have seen too many ""molecular signaling"" projects like B and C fail to deliver a final result. A is the only one with a proven track record of success.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,I feel a great sense of peace with Candidate A. It is a project that respects the reality of our current resources.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm happy we all agree. It's the most balanced choice for the agency and the researchers.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,Yay! I'm glad we're picking the one that can actually get done. I don't want anyone to be sad because their project failed!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure when logic and pragmatism align so perfectly. Candidate A is the only rational choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It is the only choice that ensures the grant is not wasted. I am satisfied with this conclusion.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
